ELIDED: (1) Bodies of the python3 heredoc scripts I wrote and ran are on disk beside this log and not pasted: build_chapters.py, build_struct.py, find.py, ctx.py, show.py, sec.py, scopedb.py, analysis.py, phrase_census.py, quotes.py, usage_scope.py, extcit_scope.py, decimal_gloss.py, final_docs.py, ledger.py, content.py, notes.py, build_deliverables.py, memo_gen.py; inline `python3 -` blocks that only read JSON or my own scratch files are summarized by the one-line "python3 inline:" entries above, not pasted. (2) find.py, ctx.py, show.py and sec.py log their own SQL and regular expression at the moment they run, but not their printed output; the printed output was read on screen and the raw document texts are kept in texts/. (3) The pipeline of reads of my own run files (ls, cat, sed -n, cut, head, tail, grep, wc, sort) and several small in-place patches of my own scripts (python3 string replacements in content.py, notes.py, quotes.py, final_docs.py, analysis.py, phrase_census.py, memo_gen.py, build_deliverables.py) are not logged line by line. (4) An early scoping listing printed full regex-hit lists (scratch_headings_latam_events.tsv, scratch_struct_sections.tsv: 153 and 106 rows) that are kept as files and not repeated here. (5) Superseded runs stay in the log above and are not removed: the first phrase_census.py run (defective AND family and a tolerant pattern narrower than strict), the first analysis.py run (control SQL failed on an attached database), the first decimal_gloss.py (country digits misread); their corrected reruns are the later entries. (6) The first, shorter list of argument documents in core_docs.txt (46 pairs) was superseded by final_docs.py (56 pairs).
